        "simplifiedParentVersion": "What this skill means:\nnavigating complex systems is about helping you and your child stay calm, understand each other, and get through tricky moments together.\n\nWhy it matters:\nWhen you use navigating complex systems, your child feels safer, more understood, and more connected to you. This makes hard moments easier for both of you.\n\nHow to use it:\n- Keep your voice calm and steady.\n- Use short, simple sentences.\n- Show your child you are listening.\n- Give clear choices when things feel stuck.\n- Take a slow breath before responding.\n\nExample:\nIf your child is upset, you might say:\n\"I'm here. Let's take a breath. We can figure this out together.\"\n\nTry this today:\nPick one small moment — like getting ready, bedtime, or a small disagreement — and practice using navigating complex systems in a calm, simple way.",
