        "closingMessage": "You do not have to get recognising triggers perfect for it to work. Children benefit from\n'good enough' parenting where adults keep coming back, repairing after mistakes,\nand trying again. Every time you pause, notice, and respond with a little more\ncalm and connection, you are already changing the story for your child.",
        "simplifiedParentVersion": "What this skill means:\nrecognising triggers is about helping you and your child stay calm, understand each other, and get through tricky moments together.\n\nWhy it matters:\nWhen you use recognising triggers, your child feels safer, more understood, and more connected to you. This makes hard moments easier for both of you.\n\nHow to use it:\n- Keep your voice calm and steady.\n- Use short, simple sentences.\n- Show your child you are listening.\n- Give clear choices when things feel stuck.\n- Take a slow breath before responding.\n\nExample:\nIf your child is upset, you might say:\n\"I'm here. Let's take a breath. We can figure this out together.\"\n\nTry this today:\nPick one small moment — like getting ready, bedtime, or a small disagreement — and practice using recognising triggers in a calm, simple way.",
